    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347-a4">

                <pb facs="0391" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg357"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 3 in No.
                    61.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Busca to Mr. de Castro.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Finance, Office of the Collector-General of
                                Customs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1897-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October 2, 1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your esteemed letter of the 23d
                    ultimo I hasten to transmit to you the inclosed circular issued by this office
                    in 1892, by which you will learn what the Italian customs office intends by
                    “clocks, so called, of American system.”</p>
                <p>Yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Busca</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >The Collector-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
